    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28523" root="عر" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَارٌّ</span></b>  A camel <i>having the mange,</i> or <i>scab;</i> as
also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعَرُّ</span></b> ; (A'Obeyd, S, O;) which latter [in
some of the copies of the K written ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَرٌّ</span></b> ] is
applied in this sense to a man; and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْرُورٌ</span></b>  to a
camel: (K:) or this last signifies <i>having,</i> or
<i>affected with, the disease called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُرّ</span>. (S, O, K.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْتَرٌّ</span>.

